This is going to change the the added test variant above:

    // The sponsor receives the payout and is not debited for the fee,
    // which comes from the ltSponsorship object. This pins the
    // FeePayerType::SponsorPreFunded early return in
    // ValidVault::feePayerAccountRoot: returning the sponsor's id there
    // instead of nullopt adds the fee back onto a balance that never paid
    // it, and the equal-amount check against the vault outflow fails. The
    // sponsor has to BE the destination for that to matter: the result is
    // only consulted by ValidVault::deltaAssetsForParty, via
    // `payer && *payer == id`, so a bystander sponsor leaves the branch
    // unexercised.
    BEAST_EXPECT(env.balance(sponsor) == sponsorBalanceBefore + XRP(100));

