🟡 **Severity: MEDIUM**

During `tfSponsorshipReassign`, `reduceReserveCount` consumes the **new** sponsor's `RemainingOwnerCount` but the **old** sponsor's `RemainingOwnerCount` on their Sponsorship object is never restored. A sponsee can repeatedly reassign objects between sponsors to permanently drain each sponsor's pre-funded reserve allocation without actually consuming new slots.
Helpful? Add 👍 / 👎

<details>
<summary>💡 Fix Suggestion</summary>

**Suggestion:** During `tfSponsorshipReassign` in the `if (!hasSignature)` block, the old sponsor's `RemainingOwnerCount` on their Sponsorship object must be restored (incremented) before the new sponsor's count is reduced. Add code to look up the old sponsor's Sponsorship SLE via `keylet::sponsorship(oldSponsorID, sponseeID)`, increment `sfRemainingOwnerCount` by `ownerCountDelta` using `applyCountDelta`, and update the view. This should be done before the existing `reduceReserveCount` call for the new sponsor.

> **⚠️ Experimental Feature**: This code suggestion is automatically generated. Please review carefully.

```suggestion
            if (!hasSignature)
            {
                // restore old sponsor's RemainingOwnerCount
                {
                    auto const oldSponsorshipSle = view().peek(
                        keylet::sponsorship(oldSponsorID, sponseeID));
                    if (!oldSponsorshipSle)
                        return tefINTERNAL;
                    auto const restoredCount = applyCountDelta(
                        oldSponsorshipSle->getFieldU32(sfRemainingOwnerCount),
                        ownerCountDelta);
                    if (!restoredCount)
                        return tefINTERNAL;
                    oldSponsorshipSle->at(sfRemainingOwnerCount) = *restoredCount;
                    view().update(oldSponsorshipSle);
                }
                // reduce new sponsor's RemainingOwnerCount
                if (auto const ter =
                        reduceReserveCount(view(), sponseeID, newSponsorID, -ownerCountDelta);
                    !isTesSuccess(ter))
                    return ter;
            }
```

</details>

