`getSponsor` for `ltRIPPLE_STATE` is not account-aware: it returns a sponsor if *either* side is sponsored, regardless of which side the querying account occupies. Capture `account` and check only the relevant sponsor field.

```suggestion:0+19
            auto const getSponsor = [&sleNode, &account]() -> std::optional<AccountID> {
                if (sleNode->isFieldPresent(sfSponsor))
                    return sleNode->getAccountID(sfSponsor);
                if (sleNode->getType() == ltRIPPLE_STATE)
                {
                    auto const highAccount =
                        sleNode->getFieldAmount(sfHighLimit).getIssuer();
                    if (account == highAccount)
                    {
                        if (sleNode->isFieldPresent(sfHighSponsor))
                            return sleNode->getAccountID(sfHighSponsor);
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        if (sleNode->isFieldPresent(sfLowSponsor))
                            return sleNode->getAccountID(sfLowSponsor);
                    }
                }
                return std::nullopt;
            };
```

Flag check is inverted: `flags & ~(tfSponsorshipTransferMask | tfUniversal)` gives bits set *outside* the valid mask — i.e., unknown/invalid flags — not the operational flags (Create/Reassign/End) that should be counted. Since `getFlagsMask()` returns `tfSponsorshipTransferMask` as the valid-flags mask (used in `preflight1` as `flags & ~(mask | tfUniversal) != 0`), this expression produces the complement of valid bits. Either `preflight1` has already zeroed those bits (popcount=0 ≠ 1 always fires, rejecting every SponsorshipTransfer), or, if called before `preflight1`, it accepts a tx with exactly one unknown flag instead of exactly one known operational flag. The check should be `flags & (tfSponsorshipCreate | tfSponsorshipReassign | tfSponsorshipEnd)` (or an equivalent operational-only submask), not `flags & ~mask`.
```suggestion
    auto const flagsSet = flags & (tfSponsorshipCreate | tfSponsorshipReassign | tfSponsorshipEnd);
    if (std::popcount(flagsSet) != 1)
```

